cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the underlying Elam atomic data; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md."
title: "X-ray Attenuation Calculator for Multicomponent Materials"
version: "1.1.0"
type: software
license: MIT
# Version 1.1.0 adds a browser version and gives the same calculated numbers as
# 1.0.0, the first stable release. These supersede the 0.1.x calculator, whose original citation (version
# DOI 10.5281/zenodo.17602371) is preserved in legacy/CITATION.cff; that script
# double-weighted mass fractions.
# The DOI below is the Zenodo *concept* DOI: it covers every version and
# resolves to the newest, so citations aggregate across releases.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.17602370
date-released: 2026-10-31
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.17602370
    description: Concept DOI, covering all versions.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23843930
    description: Version DOI for 1.0.1 specifically.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22878495
    description: Version DOI for 1.0.0 specifically.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.17602371
    description: Version DOI for the superseded 0.1.1 calculator.
authors:
  - family-names: Jalaludeen
    given-names: Mohamed Faizal Ussama
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0077-691X"
    affiliation: Aalborg University
repository-code: "https://github.com/faizalusama/X-ray_attenuation_calculator"
url: "https://faizalusama.github.io/X-ray_attenuation_calculator/"
abstract: >-
  A graphical and programmable calculator, used in a web browser or installed
  locally, for narrow-beam X-ray
  attenuation in multicomponent materials and planar multilayers: glasses,
  ceramics, composites and filters. It computes energy-dependent mass and
  linear attenuation, transmission, interaction channels, half- and
  tenth-value layers and attenuation lengths from chemical composition and
  density, with user-supplied spectra and Monte Carlo uncertainty.
keywords:
  - X-ray attenuation
  - mass attenuation coefficient
  - multicomponent materials
  - Beer-Lambert law
  - transmission
  - oxide glasses
  - ceramics
  - multilayers
  - materials science
  - X-ray scattering
  - Python
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A new atomic database for X-ray spectroscopic calculations"
    authors:
      - family-names: Elam
        given-names: W. T.
      - family-names: Ravel
        given-names: B. D.
      - family-names: Sieber
        given-names: J. R.
    journal: Radiation Physics and Chemistry
    volume: 63
    start: 121
    end: 128
    year: 2002
    doi: 10.1016/S0969-806X(01)00227-4
